            <title>[LU-20991] recovery-small test_152: QoS allocation slower than RR with LU-16330's fix in the code</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20991</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;QoS allocation took 56 seconds (threshold 20s):&lt;br/&gt;
 recovery-small test_152: @@@@@@ FAIL: QoS allocation slower than RR, killable semaphore doesn't work&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d9678ef5-ee40-4e37-858e-ade217afddd5" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d9678ef5-ee40-4e37-858e-ade217afddd5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16330" title="recovery-small test_152: QoS allocation slower than RR, killable semaphore doesn't work" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16330"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16330&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (Resolved, Fixed by change 67471) covers this same error&lt;br/&gt;
message, but the tested code (48b50ff4557d) already holds that fix:&lt;br/&gt;
this is the only one of the last 17 recovery-small test_152 failures&lt;br/&gt;
in 30 days whose build held it, so it is not that bug recurring&lt;br/&gt;
verbatim. The test's own dmesg shows a 'touch' task blocked over 122s&lt;br/&gt;
in open_last_lookups -&amp;gt; down_write, i.e. the VFS exclusive lock on the&lt;br/&gt;
shared parent directory during the test's concurrent creates, the&lt;br/&gt;
mechanism &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17295" title="avoiding VFS exclusive locking on shared parent directory in -&amp;gt;atomic_open()" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17295"&gt;LU-17295&lt;/a&gt; describes, not &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16330" title="recovery-small test_152: QoS allocation slower than RR, killable semaphore doesn't work" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16330"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16330&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;'s signal-handling issue.&lt;br/&gt;
Patch 69320 only reserves an OBD_CONNECT2 flag and adds wire-constant&lt;br/&gt;
checks; it touches none of this code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69320-ps13-720e51c94e86 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69320" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69320&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
